{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/architecture"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"Architecture","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Architecture","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppLifecycle","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/RenderCycle"],"anchor":"Essentials"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Understand the layer model and rendering pipeline of TUIkit.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"TUIkit is structured in six layers, each building on the one below. This clean separation makes the framework easy to extend and maintain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Layer-Model","type":"heading","text":"Layer Model","level":2},{"anchor":"1-App-Layer","type":"heading","text":"1. App Layer","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/App","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol is the entry point. It defines one or more scenes that make up your application. The internal "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppRunner"},{"type":"text","text":" manages the async event loop, terminal setup, signal handling, and event dispatching."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["@main → App → AppRunner → RuntimeEventChannel"]},{"anchor":"2-View-Layer","type":"heading","text":"2. View Layer","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every UI component conforms to the ","type":"text"},{"identifie